---
const brewCommands = "brew tap ChristianVilen/ku-ka\nbrew install --cask kuka";
---
<section id="hero" data-capture-zone class="cursor-crosshair touch-pan-y">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-14 px-6 pb-28 pt-16 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,5fr)] lg:gap-16 lg:pt-20">
    <div>
      <h1 class="rise font-display text-[clamp(2.5rem,4.5vw+0.75rem,4.5rem)] font-semibold leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink" style="--i:0">
        Screenshots. Tiling. Keep&nbsp;awake.
      </h1>
      <p class="rise mt-6 max-w-[55ch] text-lg text-neutral" style="--i:1">
        Ku-Ka is one lightweight menu bar app for macOS: a better
        <kbd>⇧⌘3</kbd>/<kbd>⇧⌘4</kbd> screenshot tool, hotkeys that tile
        windows, and a timer that keeps your Mac awake through long builds.
        It stays out of your Dock.
      </p>
      <div class="rise mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-7 gap-y-4" style="--i:2">
        <a href="#install" class="btn-primary px-5 py-2.5">Install with Homebrew</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/ChristianVilen/ku-ka/releases/latest" class="link-quiet">Download the .zip →</a>
      </div>
      <p class="rise mono-label mt-12" style="--i:4">
        Try it: drag anywhere, just like <kbd>⇧⌘4</kbd>
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="rise" style="--i:3">
      <div class="code-card text-sm">
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-graphite-rule px-4 py-2.5">
          <span class="mono-label text-graphite-muted!">Terminal</span>
          <button type="button" class="btn-copy" data-copy={brewCommands}>Copy</button>
        </figcaption>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed"><code><span class="text-accent-bright">$</span> brew tap ChristianVilen/ku-ka
<span class="text-accent-bright">$</span> brew install --cask kuka
<span class="text-graphite-muted"># requires macOS 14 (Sonoma) or later</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
